Version: [current]
Command: monochange init

Generate monochange.toml with detected packages and groups

[1m[97mUsage:[0m [93mmonochange init[0m [95m[OPTIONS][0m

[1m[96mOptions:[0m
      [93m--force[0m
          Overwrite an existing monochange.toml file

      [93m--provider[0m[95m [0m[95m<PROVIDER>[0m
          Source-control provider for release automation workflows

          [possible values: github, gitlab, gitea]

  [93m-h[0m, [93m--help[0m
          Print help

[1m[96mGlobal Options:[0m
  [93m-q[0m, [93m--quiet[0m
          Suppress result, progress, and diagnostic output without changing execution

  [93m-v[0m, [93m--verbose[0m
          Show full result lists and logs, every step timing, and progress notes

      [93m--color[0m[95m [0m[95m<WHEN>[0m
          Control when output uses color; `auto` honors NO_COLOR, CLICOLOR, and CLICOLOR_FORCE

          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      [93m--progress-format[0m[95m [0m[95m<FORMAT>[0m
          Control progress output on stderr

          [possible values: auto, unicode, ascii, json]

      [93m--jq[0m[95m [0m[95m<EXPRESSION>[0m
          Filter explicit JSON output; requires `--format json` or `--format json-min`

      [93m--snapshot[0m
          Print a normalized JSON snapshot for this command subtree

Examples:
  monochange init
  monochange init --provider github
  monochange init --force

With --provider, the generated config also includes:
  - a [source] section for the provider
  - release and pull request settings for the provider
  - GitHub Actions workflows (for --provider github)

The starter config does not generate [cli.*] command aliases.
